-- the multiplicity of a scope key is said when the index is built and bounded by sift.scope_max_multiplicity
SET client_min_messages = notice;
REINDEX INDEX events_col;
NOTICE:  scope "tenant_id": 21,225 entries for 18,462 rows (1.15 per row)
NOTICE:  sift_col index "events_col": 2 automatic choices (key_columns, track_changes)
DETAIL:  key_columns = dim_a_id; track_changes = id
HINT:  Reasons, costs and how to turn each off: SELECT * FROM sift.index_choices('events_col');
NOTICE:  sift_col index "events_col" has a scope: column format minor 45, which a library before 5.0 cannot read
HINT:  The scope option needs this format: build the index without it for the older library.
SET client_min_messages = warning;
SET sift.scope_max_multiplicity = 1.0;
SELECT try('REINDEX INDEX events_col') AS refused;
                                                                                                                                                  refused                                                                                                                                                   
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 scope "tenant_id": 21,225 entries for 18,462 rows (1.15 per row) is over sift.scope_max_multiplicity (1) [Above it the join answers the scope reads (the entity path); a count or a sum by key is cheaper from a table of them (docs/INDEX-RECIPES.md). SET sift.scope_max_multiplicity raises the limit.]
(1 row)

